ght. If machines prove incapable of achieving superior reliability, the case for full autonomy weakens, and we must return to a model of supervised hybrid systems. Conversely, if we accept that human intervention introduces fatal latency, then demanding human-in-the-loop requirements becomes an unethical barrier to progress. We must stop treating the human bottleneck as a safety feature and recognize it for what it is: an obsolete, inefficient interference in the evolution of our critical infrastructure. ⚡",
